      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think for clean separation what\u0027s possible over usb and what - over /dev/tpm0 there should be two wrappers around extension_route_command((), one for USB path and one for TPM path.\n\nand then each wrapper can deplty its own policy at what\u0027s allowed when, and would return error when a prohibited extension is attempted.\n\nThe rest of processing in this file would not change, so there would be no issues with forgetting to free a buffer, not returning a message to the host, etc.",
